      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1884 a fire destroyed much of Plaka, sparking excavations of the Roman Agora and Hadrian's Library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plaka",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Plaka sits on the northeast slope of the Acropolis, between Syntagma and Monastiraki squares.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plaka",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The neighborhood's utilities—water, power, internet—are all buried underground in custom tunnels, the only Athens area with this system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plaka",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1918 Museum of Traditional Greek Life showcases crafts from the 17th to 20th centuries, offering a window into everyday Greek culture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
